20
00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:44.032
<v Daniel>It was published in the journal Science Advances on September 2, 2026.</v>

21
00:01:44.392 --> 00:01:44.632
<v Maya>Right.</v>

22
00:01:44.772 --> 00:01:50.855
<v Daniel>The lead author is Tianyi Peng, working with a team of 23 researchers almost entirely based at Columbia University.</v>

23
00:01:50.875 --> 00:01:52.636
<v Maya>A very heavy hitting team. Definitely.</v>

24
00:01:53.136 --> 00:02:00.343
<v Daniel>And our mission today is to unpack this absolute mega study to see if these digital twins actually work or if we're just fooling ourselves.</v>

25
00:02:00.563 --> 00:02:05.828
<v Maya>To really frame the stakes here, you have to picture a backdrop of a vast, slightly distorted cityscape.</v>

26
00:02:05.988 --> 00:02:06.969
<v Daniel>Okay, I like that image.</v>

27
00:02:07.169 --> 00:02:15.356
